            <ArticleTitle>Symptomatic hibernoma: a rare soft tissue tumor.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>342-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hibernomas are benign soft tissue tumors containing prominent brown adipocytes that resemble normal brown fat. Hibernomas have not been associated with malignant potential; however, they are similar in clinical presentation to malignant tumors like liposarcomas. This article describes the clinical, radiographic, and histologic features of a patient with a hibernoma arising from the left superior flank.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
